case: starting (source mode STARTING)

A declared source mode the CONTRACT CANNOT EXPRESS.

PowerState declares SHUTTING_DOWN but no counterpart on the way up. Until
2026-09-04 this mapping emitted "POWER_STATE_STARTING" anyway -- a value
no enum has ever declared. Nothing caught it, because no case exercised
STARTING: the 2026-08-15 catch-all fix enumerated the ten declared source
modes but the suite only ever ran seven of them, and the four it did not
run were exactly where the invented targets hid.

This case exists so the gap cannot reopen. It pins the honest answer:
power_state UNSPECIFIED -- declining to claim, rather than substituting
"ON" and asserting an availability the source did not report.

If PowerState later gains a STARTING value, this golden is where that
change becomes visible.
